# Implementation Plan - Fix API Startup Hang & Database Connectivity

The API is currently hanging on startup while attempting to connect to Supabase. This is causing the Gunicorn workers to become unresponsive, leading to the 502/522 timeouts you are seeing. I will implement connection timeouts and SSL requirements to stabilize the backend.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Credentials**: I will update the `.env` file to include `?sslmode=require` and `?supavisor_session_mode=true` to ensure compatibility with the Supabase pooler.
> 
> [!WARNING]
> **API Timeout**: I will set a **10-second timeout** for the database connection. If the database is unreachable, the API will now fail gracefully and log the error rather than hanging indefinitely.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend Stabilization

#### [MODIFY] [database.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/api/database.py)
- Update `create_engine` to include `connect_args={"connect_timeout": 10}`. This prevents the entire application from hanging if Supabase is slow to respond.

#### [MODIFY] [.env](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/.env)
- Update `DATABASE_URL` to: `postgresql+psycopg://postgres.lcijmzschmnzghxqnpsd:SqAuTO2556hkeygen@aws-1-ap-southeast-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require`.

### 2. Docker & Gunicorn Optimization

#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/docker/Dockerfile)
- Reduce Gunicorn worker count from `4` to `2` (more suitable for a `Standard_B2s` VM).
- Add `--timeout 90` to Gunicorn to prevent silent hangs.

#### [MODIFY] [nginx.conf](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/docker/nginx.conf)
- Increase `proxy_connect_timeout` and `proxy_read_timeout` to **90 seconds** to give Next.js and the API enough time to process heavy initial connections.

